From 94ee77c3624309ab735e176abbb65e7b880acfee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <jelon@tbu.net>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 11:24:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 048/206] feat(shorebird): LinkOracle -- the runtime reader of
 the .vmcode link table
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Their class, recovered from the DWARF in Flutter.framework.dSYM: byte size 0x60,
member order and offsets, method set, signatures, enumerator values and
declaration lines all come from their debug info rather than from inference, so
each member carries the line it sits on in their header. The file pairing is
theirs too -- header at runtime/vm/shorebird/shorebird.h, implementation at
runtime/vm/shorebird.cc -- kept so the dSYM line differential stays usable.

What it does: a patch is compiled by a simulator gen_snapshot, so patch code
cannot run on the CPU. The linker pairs every patch function whose subgraph hash
is unchanged with its base counterpart and writes those pairs into the .vmcode
header; this class answers, per offset, whether a function runs the base's
native code or has to be simulated. The header layout is the one established
byte by byte in GROUND_TRUTH.md §1 (uint32 count, then count pairs of uint32),
which is what tools/linker.py already writes -- the two are ends of one contract.

Dart_ShorebirdLoadVmcode now builds one and installs it, so this is wired rather
than dead. The existing Simulator::SetPendingVmcodeFile path is untouched.

Two deliberate divergences, both marked in the header:
- Install() is ours. Their installer is in code we have not recovered, and a
  singleton nothing can populate cannot be tested.
- RunTargetFromBaseOffset is dead in their engine -- declared in DWARF with no
  inlined instance anywhere and no out-of-line symbol, the same situation as
  print_dispatch_table_debug_info_to in gen_snapshot. Its body here is the
  symmetric reading of the same table and is not verified against them.

Bounds are plain ifs, not ASSERTs: a negative or absurd entry count is rejected
before it can become an allocation, and a table that does not fit its buffer is
refused in ReadHeaderSize rather than read out of bounds in BuildCaches.

Verified: 13 new LinkOracle cases pass; all 69 shorebird-side cases pass; the
product gen_snapshot still links and still emits byte-identical .ddid. Negative
control run -- flipping the hit branch of RunTargetFromPatchOffset from cpu to
sim turns exactly two cases red, so these tests can fail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

